/*!
\page page_stisthit StIstHit

\ref StIstHit represents a single reconstructed hit (1-D strip cluster) in the STAR
Intermediate Silicon Tracker (IST), the middle layer of the HFT.  The IST is a pad-based silicon
strip detector on 24 ladders, each with 6 sensors, providing primarily r–φ position information.

\see StIstHitCollection

\section sec_isthit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
StObject
└── StMeasuredPoint
    └── StHit
        └── StIstHit
\endverbatim

Hits are collected in \ref StIstHitCollection.

\section sec_isthit_geometry IST Geometry Constants

From the <tt>StIstConsts</tt> namespace in <tt>StEnumerations.h</tt>:

- <tt>kIstNumLadders = 24</tt>
- <tt>kIstNumSensorsPerLadder = 6</tt>
- <tt>kIstNumSensors = 144</tt>
- <tt>kIstNumPadsPerSensor = 768</tt>
- <tt>kIstNumRowsPerSensor = 64</tt> (r–φ direction)
- <tt>kIstNumColumnsPerSensor = 12</tt> (z direction)

Hardware position encoding: <tt>hwPos = (ladder-1) × 6 + sensor</tt> (both 1-based).

\section sec_isthit_members Data Members

\subsection subsec_isthit_inherited Inherited from StHit

- <tt>UInt_t mHardwarePosition</tt> — Encodes ladder and sensor: <tt>(ladder-1)*6 + sensor</tt>.
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPositionError</tt> — 1-σ errors (cm). <em>Not persisted.</em>
- <tt>Float_t mCharge</tt> — Cluster charge (ADC counts).
- <tt>Int_t mId</tt> — Hit identifier.
- <tt>Int_t mIdTruth</tt> — Geant track ID (simulation only).
- <tt>UShort_t mQuality</tt> — Charge fraction from <tt>mIdTruth</tt> (percent).
- <tt>UChar_t mFitFlag</tt> — Non-zero if used in a track fit.
- <tt>UChar_t mTrackRefCount</tt> — Number of tracks referencing this hit.
- <tt>UShort_t mFlag</tt> — Hit status flag bitmask.

\subsection subsec_isthit_own Own Data Members

- <tt>UChar_t mMaxTimeBin</tt> — Time bin index with maximum charge (0-based).
- <tt>Float_t mChargeErr</tt> — Charge uncertainty (ADC counts).
- <tt>UChar_t mNRawHits</tt> — Total cluster size (number of fired pads).
- <tt>UChar_t mNRawHitsZ</tt> — Cluster size in the z direction.
- <tt>UChar_t mNRawHitsRPhi</tt> — Cluster size in the r–φ direction.
- <tt>Float_t mLocalPosition[3]</tt> — Local hit position (cm): [0] = r–φ, [1] = y (sensor normal), [2] = z.
- <tt>StDetectorId mDetectorId</tt> — Detector identifier (<tt>kIstId</tt>).
- <tt>static StMemoryPool mPool</tt> — Per-class memory pool. <em>Not persisted.</em>

\section sec_isthit_methods Key Methods

- <tt>unsigned char getLadder() const</tt> — Ladder (1–24) from <tt>mHardwarePosition</tt>.
- <tt>unsigned char getSensor() const</tt> — Sensor (1–6) from <tt>mHardwarePosition</tt>.
- <tt>unsigned char getMaxTimeBin() const</tt> — Max-charge time bin index.
- <tt>float getChargeErr() const</tt> — Charge uncertainty (ADC).
- <tt>unsigned char getNRawHits() const</tt> — Total cluster size.
- <tt>unsigned char getNRawHitsZ() const</tt> — Cluster size in z.
- <tt>unsigned char getNRawHitsRPhi() const</tt> — Cluster size in r–φ.
- <tt>float localPosition(unsigned int i) const</tt> — Local coordinate along axis <tt>i</tt> (cm).
- <tt>void setLocalPosition(float vRPhi, float vY, float vZ)</tt> — Set local position (cm).
- <tt>StDetectorId detector() const</tt> — Returns <tt>kIstId</tt>.

\section sec_isthit_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StIstHit uses a custom <tt>StMemoryPool</tt> allocator.  Ownership transfers to the
framework on insertion.
\warning Do <b>not</b> <tt>delete</tt> \ref StIstHit pointers obtained from the collection.

\section sec_isthit_usage Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StIstHitCollection* istColl = event->istHitCollection();
if (!istColl) return;

for (unsigned int iLadder = 1; iLadder <= 24; ++iLadder) {
    const StIstLadderHitCollection* ladder = istColl->ladder(iLadder - 1);
    if (!ladder) continue;
    for (unsigned int iSensor = 1; iSensor <= 6; ++iSensor) {
        const StIstSensorHitCollection* sensor = ladder->sensor(iSensor - 1);
        if (!sensor) continue;
        const StSPtrVecIstHit& hits = sensor->hits();
        for (const StIstHit* hit : hits) {
            float rPhi  = hit->localPosition(0); // r-phi direction (cm)
            float z     = hit->localPosition(2); // z direction (cm)
            unsigned char lad = hit->getLadder(); // 1–24
            unsigned char sen = hit->getSensor(); // 1–6
        }
    }
}
\endcode

*/
